WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.730
McQueen's return race!

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.330
And she dominates, as if to clear 
away any doubt about her condition!

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.530
Damn it!

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.110
There were concerns about Mejiro 
McQueen's preparation before the race,

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.110
but she had a flawless run, 
setting a record time of 2:03.03!

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.100
McQueen just ran a
picture-perfect return race.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.240
I wish I could start running again soon.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.320
It really was a perfect run, without the 
slightest sign of trouble, wasn't it?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.680
I'd certainly agree. It'll be hard not to 
get excited for a possible unprecedented

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.130
third win at the Spring Tennoushou.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.860
Why Rice Shower, though?

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.450
She just had to ruin it.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.260
I wanted to see Bourbon win the Triple Crown.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.380
What a disappointment.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.720
The champion has returned!

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.160
And her approach to the Spring 
Tennoushou is all clear!

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:05.710
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.710
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.380
Wow, you're on the cover of 
about every paper, McQueen.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.470
This is awesome, McQueen! 
You've got all eyes on you.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.890
Episode 7

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.870
I'm glad, but I must admit, it's a bit 
embarrassing to receive so much attention.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.740
"Rice Shower's management 
declares her imminent victory.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.370
'On a clear day, she will win.'"

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.820
True enough. I think the only competition 
you have in long-distance racing right now

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.130
is Rice Shower.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.700
It says that her time during 
the last three furlongs

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.220
of the Kikkashou was better than yours.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.890
There's more to racing than segment times.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.670
But fair enough. I'd be glad to take her on.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.310
I didn't let Teio have the Spring plaque.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.510
And it will be mine again.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.400
<i>Let's introduce the star horse girls 
going into the Spring Tennoushou.</i>

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.750
<i>It's fair to say that the 
spotlight is shining on</i>

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.610
<b>A CLOSE LOOK AT THE HORSE GIRLS RUNNING IN THE SPRING TENNOUSHOU!</b>

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.930
<i>Mejiro McQueen, who is hoping to win 
the race for a third consecutive time.</i>

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:04.870
<b>A CLOSE LOOK AT THE HORSE GIRLS RUNNING IN THE SPRING TENNOUSHOU!</b>

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.880
<i>People are calling her the best active racer,
and they're not exaggerating.</i>

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.680
<i>Next is Rice Shower, who foiled 
Mihono Bourbon's attempt at the Triple Crown.</i>

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>Will she put an end to another 
attempt to make history?</i>

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.750
<b>A CLOSE LOOK AT THE HORSE GIRLS RUNNING IN THE SPRING TENNOUSHOU!</b>

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.000
Rice Shower's running too, huh?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.250
This is McQueen's shot at 
a third consecutive win.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.620
Here's hoping she doesn't ruin it.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.760
Tell me about it.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.720
<i>Rice Shower took first place 
at the Nikkei Sho as well.</i>

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.220
<b>A CLOSE LOOK AT THE HORSE GIRLS RUNNING IN THE SPRING TENNOUSHOU!</b>

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.220
<i>She's bound to be in good shape 
heading towards the Spring Tennoushou.</i>

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.220
Hey, hey, hey!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.430
Is it me, or is Rice looking 
real strong lately?!

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.920
She's been working hard.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:36.190
<b>F{*\3c&HE6E0D8&}r{*\3c&HE7E1D9&}i{*\3c&HE7E1DA&}e{*\3c&HE8E2DB&}n{*\3c&HE8E3DC&}d{*\3c&HE9E4DD&}s{*\3c&HE9E5DE&}h{*\3c&HEAE6DE&}i{*\3c&HEAE6DF&}p {*\3c&HEBE8E1&}• {*\3c&HECEAE3&}E{*\3c&HECEAE4&}f{*\3c&HEDEBE5&}f{*\3c&HEDECE6&}o{*\3c&HEEEDE7&}r{*\3c&HEEEEE8&}t {*\3c&HEFEFEA&}• {*\3c&HF0F1EB&}V{*\3c&HF1F2EC&}i{*\3c&HF1F3ED&}c{*\3c&HF2F4EE&}t{*\3c&HF2F4EF&}o{*\3c&HF3F5F0&}ry</b>

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.200
I think she's got her sights 
set on taking McQueen down.

