00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.870
<i>In her last race in the G2, 
she managed to beat Rice Shower.</i>

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.280
<i>Expectations for her will be high.</i>

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.030
She did beat Rice, after all.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.820
You were all there rooting for me, remember?!

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.290
We're gonna do some godrunning 
at the Tennoushou, too!

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.830
I'm down to clown with that!

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.450
I think we might've figured 
out the trick to outrunning.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.960
For real, though! It's like, you 
gotta run hella good, right?

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.820
Coming around the second corner, it's
 Daitaku Helios and Mejiro Palmer in the lead!

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.720
Yet again, we see the two 
of them setting the pace!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.280
It's me!

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:04.910
No, me!

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.440
It's me!

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:06.630
No, me!

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:10.100
And Mejiro Palmer and Daitaku Helios
 have fallen apart!

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.440
We didn't manage to stay out in 
front during the Fall Tennoushou.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.190
We're now on the back half of the race!

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.910
Mejiro Palmer and Daitaku Helios are 
outrunning the others by a big margin!

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.780
There are over ten lengths between 
the two of them and third place!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.950
The others will have to pick 
up the pace to close this gap!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:24.690
It's me!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.320
It doesn't look like anyone is 
going to come close, though!

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.220
No, me!

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:25.780
It's me!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.950
No, me!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.960
You can take it from here!

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.450
We're BFFs!

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:33.560
<b>Nice Nature</b>

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.660
But we ran like whoa at the Arima Kinen!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.980
Rice!

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.570
Looking forward to running with 
you in the next race, Rice!

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.970
Huh?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.530
What's with her?

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.970
Not sure...

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.980
<b>Intent to Ultim-Outrun!!</b>

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.980
<b>McQueen  Setting Her Sights on a Third Consecutive Win</b>

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.980
<b>Machikane Tannhäuser and Mejiro Palmer in Top Shape!</b>

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.730
<b>Rice Shower's Management
Confident in Her Ability
 to Upset Mejiro McQueen!</b>

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.730
<b>Will the Assassin in Black 
Thwart Another Major Accomplishment?!</b>

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.230
<b>Will the Assassin in Black
\hThwart Another Major Accomplishment?!</b>

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.290
Rice Shower-san?

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.840
I was hoping to speak with you.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.980
I saw the feature you were in.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.720
You seem certain you'll be able to win.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.250
Consider the challenge accepted. 
Let's have a good race, shall we?

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.300
I'm not running in the Tennoushou.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.840
I don't want to race anymore!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.020
Hey, wait—

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.850
McQueen-san is so cool!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.180
A third championship! That'd be great to see.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.100
I'd love to see it happen!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.200
It's gonna be great!

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.120
Right?

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.320
What?

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.580
Is this for real?

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.080
Unbelievable...

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.990
It's such a shame.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.630
No one wants me around.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.000
Wait, Rice isn't running?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.480
She doesn't seem to want to run anymore.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:08.480
It's probably some scheme to get you 
to drop your guard before the race.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.500
Did something happen to her?

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.810
Her entry is still listed...

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.410
That sounds like a plan <i>you'd</i> come up with.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.760
So it's probably something personal.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.310
Excuse me?! I always run fair and square!

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.580
Hey, the less competition, the better.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.410
Do you, now?

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.060
You'll have an even easier time taking it.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:17.110
You're the one who tries to dupe 
people by faking like you got a cold!

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.390
What's wrong?

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.420
I do no such thing!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:21.930
It's a bit disappointing. I had 
heard she was looking strong.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.490
You're the one who pulls that 
"maybe I'll run, maybe not" scheme!

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:21.930
It's not a scheme!

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.770
Worrying about someone else 
won't get you anywhere.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.640
That just makes you a liar!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.660
You should focus on your training.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.540
I am not!

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.130
I suppose...

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.280
I'm going to ask her what's going on.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:30.300
Teio?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.040
You're not gonna be able to focus on 
your training with this bugging you.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.140
Leave this to your team leader!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.340
We'll go, too!

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:41.110
Right?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.040
Sounds good.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.070
I appreciate it, everyone.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.810
Found ya, Rice!

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:56.870
Nice weather today, huh?

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.870
Makes you want to get out 
there and run hard, right?

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.190
I-I guess so...

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:05.410
But if you run too much, it makes 
fixing up the track a lot of work!

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.940
<i>Huh? She's not asking about the Tennoushou?</i>

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.780
I actually wanted to ask 
you about the Tennoushou—

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.280
Hey, wait!

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.050
Look at this! I'm great at 
touching the bottom of my feet!

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:25.420
You gonna enter the Spring Ten? 
I bet it'd be a lot of fun!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.050
Probably as much fun as stretching like this!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:31.050
I actually hold a record in flexibility!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.800
Rice...

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.430
About the Spring Ten...

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:39.640
Hey!

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:43.310
This is kinda...

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.150
This looks like a job for me.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.530
I'm counting on you, Spe-chan!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:59.740
Rice Shower. What a lovely name! I'm a fan.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.540
Especially the "rice" part.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:05.540
It didn't work.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.720
I'm not sure what you were 
trying to accomplish!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.670
I guess we'll have to 
try the direct approach!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.060
Wh-Who are you?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.860
Scarlet! Vodka! Spe! Get 'er, girls!

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.610
Right, Gold Ship-san!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.270
It's Spica!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.620
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.230
Um... wh-what is this?

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.080
Sorry about this, Rice.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.950
McQueen told us you weren't 
going to run in the Tennoushou.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.000
Would you tell us about it?

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.170
Will you let me go if I do?

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.620
Because there's no point.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.720
What do you mean?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.880
Because no one wants me around.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:06.570
Ever since I was little, I used to look 
up to things that were glamorous.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.100
<b>The two of them were blessed

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.110
<b>The two of them were blessed

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.110
<b>The Magic of Happiness</b>

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.360
There are 100 meters to go! 
First place has a tiny lead!

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.190
Number 8, Rice Shower, is in 
front by a small margin!

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.870
And Rice Shower crosses the 
goal with her lead intact!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:25.100
Rice Shower has done a fine 
job of winning her debut race!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.280
I was so glad when I won my first race...

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.280
And everyone was really happy.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.210
It made running seem like so much fun.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.760
I thought that even someone 
like me could be glamorous.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.950
She's striking an imposing figure!

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.720
Mihono Bourbon manages to outrun the 
entire pack as she crosses the goal!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.840
She wins the Satsukishou while undefeated!

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:51.620
Bourbon-san was so dazzling 
when she won the Satsukishou...

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:56.080
So I decided I wanted 
to be like her someday.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.910
Mihono Bourbon is in the lead! 
It's looking like she has this race won!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.780
I wanted to catch up with 
the person I idolized.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.780
I wanted to win a race, 
and be like Bourbon-san.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.840
And then, at the Kikkashou, 
it finally happened..

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:13.050
Mihono Bourbon is in the lead!

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.070
Rice Shower is closing the gap! 
Mihono Bourbon still has a faint lead!

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:18.830
But Rice Shower moves up on the outside!
 Rice Shower passes her!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.760
Rice Shower has the lead! 
And she clears the goal!

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:21.760
Kikkashou

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.670
Mihono Bourbon's Triple Crown 
will remain incomplete!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:28.070
The winning horse girl of the 
Kikkashou is Rice Shower!

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.090
Wait, what?

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:30.970
What the heck?

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:31.840
Seriously?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.820
I wanted to see a Triple Crown.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.980
Why?

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:43.440
Nobody wanted me to win.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.790
Why didn't Bourbon win?

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.010
I destroyed Bourbon-san 
and her fans' dreams.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.000
Everyone was sad.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:11:00.370
Now everyone is looking forward to 
McQueen-san winning a third Spring Tennoushou.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:04.530
Even if I enter and win, 
no one will be happy.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.820
I'll just make everyone miserable.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.980
Me, whose name is supposed to 
represent something happy.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.430
<i>That's... really heavy.</i>

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:15.070
So I won't be running anymore.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:15.980
Rice?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.230
Please, leave me alone.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.430
Rice...

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.500
I had no idea.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.630
I understand how she feels!

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.650
She worked so hard on her racing,

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.980
so it has to be frustrating for no 
one to recognize what she accomplished!

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:43.740
True enough, Rice's Kikkashou win is 
something that should have been celebrated.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.630
But...

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.820
I believe using that as a reason 
to turn away from racing is,

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:50.280
for a horse girl, mistaken.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.840
McQueen...

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.070
Okay!

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.570
I'll try and convince Rice to run after all.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.180
Just don't regret this, okay?

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.340
I would never.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:10.200
Besides, I find it vexing to 
have Rice taking me so lightly.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.710
"No one will be happy if I win"?

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.380
She's so certain of her victory,
 before even running.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:17.710
Now that you mention it...

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.970
Please take care of things with Rice, Leader.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.970
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.970
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:25.250
Sure!

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.520
<i>I said that, but...</i>

